'''Zorby's Western Shiplot'''<ref name="Kassa Story Gallery">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e1-story-gallery|text="Kassa" Story Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 9}}</ref>, or just '''Zorby's Shiplot'''<ref name="Kassa Trivia Guide">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e1-trivia-gallery|text="Kassa" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 5}}</ref>, was a [[starship]] lot on the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]]. The business was run by an individual named [[Zorby]], who had hired a [[human]] named [[Pegla]] to patrol the area with [[Corellian hound]]s. In [[5 BBY]], Pegla went behind his boss' back and allowed his friend, [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], to secretly borrow a [[Breon HOY-39 Dayvan|Breon Dayvan]] for an undisclosed purpose. When Andor returned the next [[Standard day|day]], Pegla found him changing the ship’s [[ID chip log]] and insisted that he leave and not return.<ref name="Kassa" />

In addition to the Dayvan, Zorby's Western Shiplot housed a number of other starships. Among them were vessels such as a [[BTL-A4 Y-wing assault starfighter/bomber]], a [[D-85 freighter]], a [[WTK-85A interstellar transport]], a [[Lancer-class pursuit craft|''Lancer''-class pursuit craft]], a [[KGZ-54 Starcrane]],<ref name="Kassa Trivia Guide" /> and a [[VCX-100 light freighter]].<ref name="Kassa" />

{{Stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Zorby's Western Shiplot first appeared in "[[Kassa (episode)|Kassa]]," the first episode of the [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]''<ref name="Kassa" /> which aired on [[September 21]], [[2022]].<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|cKOegEuCcfw|Andor &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+ (2:25)|sw_url=video/andor-official-trailer}}</ref> It was later identified by name in the associated episode guide on [[StarWars.com]].<ref name="Kassa Story Gallery" />

